{
  "summary": "Adds wallet and RPC support for sending transactions to BIP 352 Silent Payment addresses. It introduces a PaymentDestination abstraction to accommodate destinations whose output scripts are derived dynamically from transaction inputs, updates coin selection to ensure derivation-eligible inputs are included, and adds output key derivation to transaction creation. The PR also persists recipient metadata to wallet storage to support fee-bumping via RBF and adds the scantxforsilentpayments RPC to scan transactions for Silent Payment outputs.",
  "problem": "Bitcoin Core cannot construct transactions paying to BIP 352 Silent Payment addresses, nor can it bump fees on such transactions if created. Users who want receiver privacy and address reuse prevention cannot use Bitcoin Core to pay Silent Payment recipients.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description notes it is a core component of BIP 352 integration tracked in issue #28536 and the second iteration of PR #28201.",
    "BIP 352 recipient outputs depend on the private keys of spending inputs; without the coin selection and key aggregation logic introduced here, standard wallet flows cannot derive valid recipient taproot outputs."
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#35301"
    ],
    "enables": [
      "#32966"
    ]
  },
  "scope_notes": "Touches sensitive wallet spending and coin selection internals across wallet/spend.cpp and wallet/feebumper.cpp. Adds a new database key 'sprecipients' and a compatibility mechanism that prevents older Bitcoin Core versions from RBF bumping silent payment transactions. Includes over 1,800 lines of tests, benchmarks, and functional testing.",
  "changed_since_previous": "",
  "card": "Adds wallet and RPC support for sending to BIP 352 Silent Payment addresses across send, sendtoaddress, sendmany, and sendall. Currently, Bitcoin Core wallet users cannot pay Silent Payment recipients, restricting adoption of receiver privacy features. The PR updates coin selection to ensure private keys are available for BIP 352 derivation, dynamically derives recipient taproot outputs, persists recipient metadata in the wallet database for RBF fee bumping, and adds the scantxforsilentpayments RPC. This work is tracked under project issue #28536 and depends on prerequisite PR #35301 while unblocking receiving support in PR #32966.",
  "needs": [
    "rest_of_diff"
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "uncertainties": [],
  "risk": {
    "level": "high",
    "touches": [
      "wallet",
      "wallet_storage",
      "rpc_api"
    ],
    "why": "Flaws in input private key aggregation or output tweak derivation could generate unspendable or unfindable taproot outputs, causing irreversible loss of user funds, while wallet database errors could break transaction state or fee bumping."
  }
}
